From f4df5543fd14a5189c1b33941cb13a6c1c09163d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 07:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 67/68] vulkan/wsi: Horizon, a deferred dependency the driver
 refuses is an error
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 8 (Correct fence-based synchronisation at
 acquire and present)
Why: wsi_horizon_create_acquire_sync returned create_wait_sync's result
 unchanged, and one of that result's values means the opposite thing on
 the two sides of the call.
 .
 Out of create_wait_sync, VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT means "these
 fences are not something I can express": the importer answers it for a
 count it cannot carry and for a set that is entirely blank. Out of this
 function it means "there is nothing outstanding", and 0064's caller
 acts on that by signalling the application's semaphore immediately.
 .
 So passing it through converts a dependency the driver DECLINED into a
 dependency that was never there — on the one path that deliberately did
 not wait for it. The application renders into a buffer the compositor
 is still reading. Nothing reports it; it is a torn frame and no error
 anywhere.
 .
 The function's own comment already promised this ("A FAILURE IS NOT
 DOWNGRADED TO THAT"); the code did not keep the promise for this
 particular failure. Raised in review of the branch.
 .
 No path reaches it today with the Horizon importer: the count is
 bounded above by ARRAY_SIZE(mf->fences) = 4 = NVKMD_MAX_SYNCPT_FENCES
 four lines up, every entry is marked valid there, and a NULL op cannot
 be reached because gpu_acquire_wait is what tests for one. Caught
 anyway — "no caller does that yet" is not the contract, and a second
 importer or a fifth fence would arrive as silence.
Evidence: CROSS BUILD, scripts/ci-build-archives.sh over
 ghcr.io/d3fau4/nx-dev:latest (aarch64-none-elf-gcc 15.2.0, meson
 1.11.2, -Wall -Wextra -Werror): wsi_horizon.c compiles with no warning
 and libvulkan_wsi.a links.
 The new branch is not reachable from any test, by construction — it is
 the case the four bounds above exclude — so nothing exercises it and
 that is stated rather than implied. NO CONSOLE HAS RUN THIS.
Upstream: no — it is a Horizon-only backend answering a Horizon-only
 driver hook.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
index 5c86692..c46fbc6 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
@@ -1958,8 +1958,44 @@ wsi_horizon_create_acquire_sync(const struct wsi_swapchain *wsi_chain,
       fences[i].valid = true;
    }
 
-   return chain->base.wsi->horizon.create_wait_sync(chain->base.device,
-                                                    fences, count, sync_out);
+   const VkResult result =
+      chain->base.wsi->horizon.create_wait_sync(chain->base.device,
+                                                fences, count, sync_out);
+
+   /* THE ONE RESULT THAT MUST NOT BE PASSED ON, and the reason it is
+    * caught here rather than trusted not to happen.
+    *
+    * VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT means two different things on the two
+    * sides of this call. Coming out of create_wait_sync it means "these
+    * fences are not something I can express" — the importer answers it
+    * for a count it cannot carry, and for a set that is entirely blank.
+    * Going out of THIS function it means "there is nothing outstanding",
+    * and wsi_common.c acts on it by signalling the application's
+    * semaphore immediately.
+    *
+    * Returning it unchanged would turn the first into the second: a
+    * dependency the driver declined to take, reported as a dependency
+    * that was never there, on an acquire that deliberately did not wait
+    * for it. The application would then render into a buffer the
+    * compositor is still reading — which is not an error anywhere, just
+    * a torn frame.
+    *
+    * No path through nvk_wsi_create_wait_sync reaches it today: the
+    * count is bounded above by ARRAY_SIZE(mf->fences) = 4 =
+    * NVKMD_MAX_SYNCPT_FENCES, every entry is marked valid four lines up,
+    * and a NULL op cannot be reached because gpu_acquire_wait is what
+    * checks for one. It is caught anyway, because the whole of this
+    * function's contract is that a deferred dependency is never
+    * downgraded, and "no caller does that yet" is not that contract.
+    */
+   if (result == VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT) {
+      mesa_loge("wsi_horizon: the driver declined a deferred release fence "
+                "(%" PRIu32 " fence(s)); nothing has waited for it",
+                count);
+      return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR;
+   }
+
+   return result;
 }
 
 static VkResult
-- 
2.43.0

